layer.current {"name": "notes"}
mtext {"at": [15, 70], "text": "NOTES\\P1. SW2 OFF before connecting USB: the on-board USB LDO (3.3 V) would push current back into the cell.\\P2. A0 must stay unconnected (ADC_VCC): the firmware reads VCC with ADC_MODE(ADC_VCC).\\P3. C1 + C2 in series = 1.65 F / 5.4 V. R1 limits the cell current (<= 45 mA at insertion, then < 5 mA), tau = 112 s.\\P4. JP1 closed = battery mode: a press pulls RST low and wakes U1 from deep sleep. JP1 open = always_on (USB).\\P5. U1 is fed directly on its 3V3 pin (on-board LDO bypassed). Standby 0.2-0.3 mA => about 4-6 weeks per CR2032.\\P6. GPIO2 drives the LED already on the D1 mini (active-low): one blink per publish. SW1 pressed = GPIO5 LOW.", "height": 2.5, "width": 232, "attach": 1, "lineSpacing": 1.15}
zoom {"mode": "extents"}
